-## Context
-
-- **Reason**: The user wants one AI Supervisor to manage other AI agents through
-  separate ACP sessions, not merely re-prompt one active chat.
-- **Priority**: correctness and safety > recoverability > observability > speed
-  > visual polish.
-- **Executor**: AI agent without human review after every implementation step.
-- **Created**: 2026-07-10, Asia/Saigon.
-- **Active branch at research time**: `master`.
-- **Worktree condition at research time**: dirty, with 92 modified or untracked
-  paths. Existing user changes must be preserved.
-- **Previous feature artifact**: `supervisos-goal.md` covers the MiniMax,
-  Scope Resolver, and Goal Mode foundation but not full multi-session
-  orchestration.
-
-### Product Definition
-
-A Supervisos run is a project-scoped control-plane object. MiniMax-M3 may
-propose a task graph and semantic decisions, but deterministic application
-services own validation, state transitions, session creation, scheduling,
-permission enforcement, workspace isolation, patch integration, retries,
-budgets, and terminal status.
-
-A worker is an independent ACP-backed chat session with its own `chatId` and,
-when available, agent-side `sessionId`. Workers may use the same configured
-agent implementation or different configured agents. The Supervisor model is
-not allowed to invent commands, executable paths, credentials, or agent IDs.
